   "subject": "Re: Difference in DWLS estimator model fit in case of numeric and ordered data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Declaring the variables ordinal vs declaring them numeric / continuous changes the data--so why shouldn&#39;t the results change? Declared numeric, a &quot;2&quot; is halfway between a &quot;1&quot; and a &quot;3.&quot; Declared ordinal, a &quot;2&quot; is *somewhere* between a &quot;1&quot; and a &quot;3.&quot;<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Oct 13, 2017 at 3:10 PM, Pawel Jurek <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">pawel...@ie-tc.pl</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
