  {
   "id": "413EeH3_AQAJ",
   "from": "Edward Rigdon",
   "author": "99a06696c483481a",
   "date": "2017-10-14T21:06:33Z",
   "subject": "Re: Difference in DWLS estimator model fit in case of numeric and ordered data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">     The polychoric correlation only makes sense if data are ordinal. If data re continuous, there would be no good reason to discretize the data for purposes of computing a polychoric correlation matrix. Such an approach would sacrifice information.<div>     For information about lavaan in particular, the lavaan project is a very good source:</div><div><a href=\"http://lavaan.ugent.be/resources/teaching.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lavaan.ugent.be/resources/teaching.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426537606000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EaI9Ipw_Ej65N2zoFWjXQ\">http://lavaan.ugent.be/resources/teaching.html<br></a></div><div><br></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sat, Oct 14, 2017 at 3:03 AM, Pawel Jurek <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">pawel...@ie-tc.pl</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Thank you\r\nEdward for answering. Of course I understand the difference between these two\r\ntypes of data. Nevertheless, I wonder what technical solutions underlie the cfa\r\nfunction in lavaan. I mean, does the cfa function using</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> a polychoric\r\ncorrelation matrix, and diagonally weighted least squares</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Calibri\">in both cases? What\r\nis the technical difference in the DWLS estimation? Is there any manual / paper\r\nin which I can read about it?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Regards,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Paweł<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<br>W dniu piątek, 13 października 2017 22:50:33 UTC+2 użytkownik Edward Rigdon napisał:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Declaring the variables ordinal vs declaring them numeric / continuous changes the data--so why shouldn&#39;t the results change? Declared numeric, a &quot;2&quot; is halfway between a &quot;1&quot; and a &quot;3.&quot; Declared ordinal, a &quot;2&quot; is *somewhere* between a &quot;1&quot; and a &quot;3.&quot;<div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Oct 13, 2017 at 3:10 PM, Pawel Jurek <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">pawel...@ie-tc.pl</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Times\">Can anyone explain why using DWLS estimator for the\r\nsame data and the same model, gives another results when data are declared as\r\nnumeric and ordered factors?</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Times\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Times\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Times\">Here an example with such difference:</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Times\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Times\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">library(lavaan)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">load(file = &quot;./data.Rda&quot;)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">model = &quot;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">  F1 =~ KE3 + KE4 + KE5 + KE6 + KE8 +\r\nKE9 + KE10 + KE11 + KE12</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">  F2 =~ KS3 + KS4 + KS6 + KS7 + KS10\r\n+ KS11 + KS12 + KS13</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">  F1 ~~ F2</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">&quot;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">fit_num &lt;- cfa(model = model, data =\r\ndata_num, estimator = &quot;DWLS&quot;)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">summary(fit_num)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">fitmeasures(object = fit_num, fit.measures\r\n= c(&quot;chisq&quot;, &quot;cfi&quot;, &quot;tli&quot;))</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span><span style=\"color:black;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:9pt\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">fit_ord_2 &lt;- cfa(model = model, data =\r\ndata_ord)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">summary(fit_ord_2)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:black\">fitmeasures(object\r\n= fit_ord_2, fit.measures = c(&quot;chisq&quot;, &quot;cfi&quot;,\r\n&quot;tli&quot;))</span>    <span><font color=\"#888888\"><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426537606000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Fxprg445FedaJZLV95m4f\">https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426537606000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0nebRU8uHtpLaPZQNoLQhG\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></font></span></blockquote></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
